1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,049
At twenty dollars an hour,

2
00:00:02,089 --> 00:00:03,751
a million dollars takes you

3
00:00:03,791 --> 00:00:05,528
twenty-four years of work.

4
00:00:05,568 --> 00:00:06,366
That's full time,

5
00:00:06,406 --> 00:00:07,930
saving every cent.

6
00:00:07,970 --> 00:00:08,781
Pay your taxes:

7
00:00:08,821 --> 00:00:10,132
twenty-eight years.

8
00:00:10,172 --> 00:00:10,983
Pay rent and save

9
00:00:11,023 --> 00:00:12,473
a normal twenty percent:

10
00:00:12,513 --> 00:00:14,249
a hundred and forty.

11
00:00:14,289 --> 00:00:16,651
Meanwhile, prices roughly double.

12
00:00:16,691 --> 00:00:18,628
Feels like a rigged game, right?

13
00:00:18,668 --> 00:00:19,766
It isn't.

14
00:00:19,806 --> 00:00:21,969
You're using the wrong equation.

15
00:00:22,009 --> 00:00:23,658
Salary is time times rate,

16
00:00:23,698 --> 00:00:25,434
and both have a ceiling.

17
00:00:25,474 --> 00:00:26,924
The other equation is

18
00:00:26,964 --> 00:00:28,613
problems solved times people reached,

19
00:00:28,653 --> 00:00:30,390
and it has no ceiling.

20
00:00:30,430 --> 00:00:31,666
A yoga teacher at

21
00:00:31,706 --> 00:00:33,156
a hundred dollars an hour

22
00:00:33,196 --> 00:00:34,294
still sells hours.

23
00:00:34,334 --> 00:00:35,345
Film the class once,

24
00:00:35,385 --> 00:00:37,122
and thousands can buy it.

25
00:00:37,162 --> 00:00:38,686
The game isn't rigged.

26
00:00:38,726 --> 00:00:40,888
You were just taught half the rules.

27
00:00:40,928 --> 00:00:43,017
Subscribe for the other half.
